### Current State

**Frontend (search-admin-ui)**:
- Uses axios client at `/src/lib/api/client.ts` with base URL `http://localhost:8080`
- Existing hooks use `/_dsearch/dictionary/*` endpoints (Elasticsearch plugin API)
- Uses React Query for state management with well-structured query keys
- TypeScript types already exist for Dictionary operations in `/src/types/index.ts`
- Auth store manages `token` and `clusterId` headers

**Backend (search-admin - Spring Boot)**:
- Base path: `/api/v1/dictionary`
- Different endpoint structure than current frontend expectations
- Response DTOs: `DictionaryWithId`, `CompileResult`

### Key Differences

| Aspect | Current Frontend (ES Plugin) | Target Backend (Spring Boot) |
|--------|------------------------------|------------------------------|
| Base Path | `/_dsearch/dictionary` | `/api/v1/dictionary` |
| List Endpoint | `GET /{type}?page&pageSize&search` | `GET /{type}?page&size` |
| Search | Query params in list | Separate `/{type}/search` endpoint |
| Create | `POST /{type}` | `POST /` with type in body |
| Update | `PUT /{type}/{id}` | `PUT /{id}` |
| Delete | `DELETE /{type}` with body | `DELETE /{id}` |
| Compile | `POST /compile` with types array | `POST /compile/{type}` or `POST /compile` |

